---
source: crates/wolf_sema/tests/conc_diagnostics.rs
expression: "render_types(&[(&[], \"main.lu\", src)])"
---
error[E1103]: `when` blocks do not nest
  --> mem:///main.lu:8:9
   |
 7 |     when (a, b) {
   |     -------------
 8 |         when (c, d) {
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 9 |             total = a + b + c + d
10 |         }
   | ^^^^^^^^^ this would acquire while a set is already held
11 |     }
   | ----- the enclosing `when` holds its whole set here
   |
   = note: `when` acquires its entire operand set at once, in one canonical order — that is what
     makes lock-order deadlock impossible ([conc.when.nodeadlock]); a nested `when` is
     incremental acquisition by another spelling. Merge the operands into the outer set
     (`when (a, b, c) { … }`), or end the outer block before acquiring the next set.
